       <h1>170 Defence Personnel Arrive in Sri Lanka for Annual 'MITRA SHAKTI' Exercise</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Military Exercise</span> <span>#Sri Lanka</span></div>
       <p>A contingent of 170 defence personnel has arrived in Sri Lanka to participate in the annual bilateral military exercise, ‘MITRA SHAKTI’, as reported by News On AIR. This deployment marks a continuation of the regular joint drills between the two nations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/170-defence-personnel-arrive-in-sri-lanka-for-annual-mitra-s.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The exercise, known as ‘MITRA SHAKTI’, is an annual event designed to foster military cooperation and strengthen bilateral ties. The arrival of the defence personnel in Sri Lanka underscores the ongoing commitment to these joint training initiatives.</p><p>What to watch: Updates on the commencement and duration of the ‘MITRA SHAKTI’ military exercise.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and accurately reflects the provided summary of the military exercise.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
