     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Economic Times · 2026-11-13 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Air India Unaffected by Microsoft Outage, IndiGo Reports Email Disruption</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Business</span> <span>#Tech Outage</span></div>
       <p>Air India announced on Friday that its flight operations remain normal despite the ongoing global Microsoft outage, with no disruptions reported in its communication channels. The airline confirmed it is closely monitoring the situation and has temporarily rerouted its emails to ensure continuous receipt of customer messages, assuring a response within its standard 24-hour timeline. All customer support avenues, including voice, AI.g, social media, and customer notifications, are functioning as expected, according to Air India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/air-india-unaffected-by-microsoft-outage-indigo-reports-emai.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In contrast, IndiGo reported that its email support services have been impacted by the widespread Microsoft disruption, potentially hindering its ability to receive customer emails. The airline advised passengers requiring urgent assistance to utilize its AI assistant, 6E Skai, accessible via its website or mobile application, while confirming that all other support channels remain operational. Both airlines have expressed apologies for any inconvenience caused and are actively monitoring developments.</p><p>The Microsoft outage is a major global event, affecting several key services including Teams, Outlook, OneDrive, and its artificial intelligence tool, Copilot. Users across various regions have reported significant difficulties accessing these essential tools for daily communication and work. Microsoft has indicated observing partial recovery in some regions following adjustments, but these measures have not yet resulted in a sustained restoration of services.</p><p>Consequently, Microsoft is exploring alternative strategies to enhance infrastructure capacity and resolve persistent traffic management issues, without providing a specific timeline for full service restoration. Outage-monitoring platform Downdetector recorded a peak of nearly 140,000 global reports concerning Outlook problems around 18:00 GMT on Thursday. Air India reiterated its commitment to assisting passengers throughout this period.</p><p>What to watch: Microsoft's progress on full service restoration.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Well-structured report covering all major points from the source text, though it contains a minor OCR typo ('AI.g' instead of 'AI') present in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/transportation/airlines-/-aviation/air-india-assures-passengers-flight-operations-unaffected-amid-microsoft-global-outage/articleshow/135792562.cms" rel="noopener">Economic Times</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-11-13/air-india-unaffected-by-microsoft-outage-indigo-reports-emai" data-title="Air India Unaffected by Microsoft Outage, IndiGo Reports Email Disruption"><b>Share:</b>
