     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-13 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Andhra Pradesh Leads Rooftop Solar Drive as India Hits 175 GW Capacity</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Minister Pralhad Joshi announced that Andhra Pradesh has enabled 7.86 lakh households to adopt rooftop solar systems. Nationally, India has successfully raised solar capacity from 2.80 GW in 2014 to 175 GW, meeting a peak power demand of 270 GW without interruption. Currently, 33% of the nation's power is sourced from non-fossil fuels.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/andhra-pradesh-leads-rooftop-solar-drive-as-india-hits-175-g.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Under the PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojana, 66 lakh households across India have benefited from solar installations. The country remains on track to achieve a 500 GW non-fossil fuel capacity target by 2030. Officials emphasized that green energy is central to India's goal of becoming a global hub for green manufacturing.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate but conflates the source's '55% non-fossil fuel capacity' with the '33% power sourced from non-fossil fuels' statistic, which could be clarified.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/andhra-pradesh-emerges-as-a-leader-in-indias-rooftop-solar-push-union-minister/article71697838.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
