       <h1>Camp Snap Releases Miniature CS-8 Micro Keychain Camera</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Camp Snap has launched the CS-8 Micro, a three-inch, 1.5-ounce screen-free digital camcorder designed to fit on a keychain. Available for $39.99 through the company's website and Urban Outfitters, the device is sold in mystery boxes with varying color rarities. It features an LCD viewfinder and captures 720p video with 8x digital zoom and five built-in filters.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/camp-snap-releases-miniature-cs-8-micro-keychain-camera.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Unlike its predecessors, the Micro requires a USB-C connection or card reader to transfer footage from its included 4GB microSD card. The device offers an estimated 30 to 45 minutes of battery life per charge, providing a portable, retro-styled filming experience.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Clear and captures all technical specifications effectively.</p>
