       <h1>ElevenLabs Launches ElevenAI Meeting and Dictation App</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Voice AI firm ElevenLabs has introduced an experimental app called ElevenAI, designed for team-based meeting note-taking and dictation. Currently in preview, the tool integrates with the company’s agent platforms to automate follow-up tasks like drafting emails and recalling details from past conversations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/elevenlabs-launches-elevenai-meeting-and-dictation-app.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>ElevenAI supports dictation in over 90 languages and is trained to recognize industry-specific terminology. The company, valued at $22 billion, is positioning the app as an enterprise solution to centralize knowledge management. Alongside this release, ElevenLabs debuted its v3 Scribe speech-to-text models, which allow companies to fine-tune transcription capabilities using their own data.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately reports the launch of ElevenAI and the v3 Scribe models based on the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
