       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Harsimrat Badal Pledges Drug-Free Punjab if SAD Wins 2027 Election</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Shiromani Akali Dal (SAD) leader Harsimrat Kaur Badal has vowed to eradicate Punjab's drug menace if the party returns to power in 2027. Accusing the current AAP government and previous Congress administration of failing to curb trafficking, Badal claimed drugs are now being delivered to homes.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/harsimrat-badal-pledges-drug-free-punjab-if-sad-wins-2027-el.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>To combat the crisis, Badal proposed a special task force led by a female DGP, harsher legal penalties including 10-year bail denials for offenders, and comprehensive rehabilitation programs. She also encouraged the formation of &quot;Mai Bhago di Fauj&quot; village groups to monitor and expose drug dealers while protecting affected families.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the core political pledges and proposed policy changes accurately and concisely.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/punjab-drug-menace-harsimrat-badal-sad-2027-task-force-ptag-3038305-2026-11-13?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
