     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-13 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>HDFC Mutual Fund Unveils Hybrid Long-Short SIF, NFO Closes November 27</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Personal Finance</span> <span>#Investment</span> <span>#Mutual Fund</span> <span>#HDFC</span></div>
       <p>HDFC Mutual Fund has entered the specialised investment fund (SIF) segment with its H-SIF Hybrid Long-Short Fund, which opened for subscription on November 13 and will close on November 27, 2026. This offering combines investments in debt and equity securities with derivatives and limited short positions, as reported by Livemint Money. The minimum investment for this new fund offer (NFO) is ₹10 lakh across SIF strategies at the Permanent Account Number (PAN) level, though accredited investors can invest a minimum of ₹10,000.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/hdfc-mutual-fund-unveils-hybrid-long-short-sif-nfo-closes-no.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The fund's strategy involves a core portfolio of relatively high-safety debt papers, arbitrage positions, and investments in real estate investment trusts (REITs) and infrastructure investment trusts (InvITs). Alongside this, the fund will utilise derivatives for hedging, earning option premiums, and taking short positions of up to 25% of its net assets. It may also participate selectively in corporate events such as initial public offerings (IPOs), share buybacks, open offers, and mergers, aiming to generate returns through multiple sources like interest income and arbitrage spreads.</p><p>Designed for flat, mildly rising, and volatile markets, the fund recommends a preferred investment horizon of more than 18 months. Redemptions are available only twice a week, on Mondays and Wednesdays, with an exit load of 0.5% applying to units redeemed or switched out within 90 days of allotment, according to the fund house. The fund is managed by Paul S Parampreet and Ihab Dalwai for equities, Anil Bamboli for debt, and Gopal Agrawal for overseas investments.</p><p>Investments in SIFs carry relatively higher risks, including potential loss of capital, liquidity risk, and market volatility, as cautioned by HDFC Mutual Fund. The flexibility of such funds, including short positions, means investors should understand how these strategies, along with debt and arbitrage investments, could affect the portfolio during different market conditions. The objective of generating returns through multiple sources does not guarantee positive returns or protect invested capital, and investors should review the investment strategy information document carefully.</p><p>What to watch: Monitor the fund's performance and asset growth in the SIF segment.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is comprehensive, accurately incorporating all technical details, manager names, and risk disclosures from the full text provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
