     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-11-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Criticizes Pakistan’s Indus Valley Claims Ahead of SCO Forum</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Culture Minister Gajendra Singh Shekhawat dismissed Pakistan's attempts to claim the ancient Indus Valley civilization, noting the nation was formed only 80 years ago. The comments preceded the inaugural SCO Civilisational Dialogue Forum, set for November 20-22 at New Delhi’s Purana Quila, where India will highlight its 5,000-year-old history.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/india-criticizes-pakistans-indus-valley-claims-ahead-of-sco-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Fifteen countries have confirmed attendance for the event, which focuses on art, architecture, and cultural traditions. India invited 25 nations, including Pakistan, though Islamabad has not yet responded to the invitation. Prime Minister Narendra Modi is scheduled to inaugurate the forum, which aims to reinforce cultural dialogue despite existing geopolitical tensions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately reflects the minister's comments and the upcoming forum details, though 'Operation Sindoor' is mentioned in the source without context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pakistan-80-years-old-cant-appropriate-indus-valley-civilisation-culture-minister/articleshow/135816035.cms" rel="noopener">Times of India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
