       <h1>India, Sri Lanka Begin Joint Military Exercise Mitra Shakti 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India</span> <span>#Sri Lanka</span> <span>#Military Exercise</span> <span>#Mitra Shakti</span></div>
       <p>India and Sri Lanka have commenced the 12th edition of their joint military exercise, Mitra Shakti 2026. The exercise marks another iteration of the bilateral defence cooperation between the two nations, as reported by The Times of India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/india-sri-lanka-begin-joint-military-exercise-mitra-shakti-2.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Mitra Shakti is a recurring joint military exercise designed to enhance interoperability and cooperation between the armed forces of India and Sri Lanka. This year's event represents the twelfth time the two countries have engaged in this specific training initiative.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on the scope and objectives of the exercise as they emerge.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and accurately reflects the provided summary; it is appropriately brief given the limited source material.</p>
