       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Indian Ambassador visits seafarer injured in MSV Quba attack</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Indian Ambassador to Oman Prashant Pise visited an injured Indian seafarer at Sohar hospital on November 12 following an October 29 attack on the vessel MSV Quba. The ship, sailing from the UAE to Somalia, was struck by an unidentified aerial object off the Omani coast, injuring several of the 13 Indian crew members.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/indian-ambassador-visits-seafarer-injured-in-msv-quba-attack.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Indian Embassy reaffirmed its commitment to supporting the affected families and seafarers. India has recently urged for safe navigation through the Strait of Hormuz, following multiple attacks on commercial shipping in the region, including a separate fatal incident near Limah on November 2.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a clear summary of the incident and the diplomatic response, though it relies on the source's provided date.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
