       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Mongabay India · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Migrants and elephants face shared risks in West Bengal's flood-prone charlands</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#environment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Residents of Premganj char in West Bengal face dual threats from recurring floods and roaming male elephant groups. The 2023 glacial lake outburst flood from South Lhonak Lake severely impacted the region, flushing industrial toxins and military debris downstream, causing health concerns among locals. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/migrants-and-elephants-face-shared-risks-in-west-bengals-flo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Experts note that maljuria elephant groups frequently explore these transient landscapes in search of food, often following routes established by younger males. As a highly vulnerable area, the settlement remains caught between environmental disasters and wildlife encounters, creating a climate of persistent uncertainty for its inhabitants.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the environmental and wildlife challenges in the Premganj charland using the provided details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://india.mongabay.com/2026/11/no-land-to-call-their-own-migrants-and-elephants-coexist-on-a-transient-landscape/" rel="noopener">Mongabay India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
