     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pakistan U19 to Face India U19 in ACC Men's U19 Asia Cup 2026 Final</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#U19 Asia Cup</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Pakistan</span></div>
       <p>Pakistan Under-19 (PAK U19) will clash with India Under-19 (IND U19) in the final of the ACC Men's U19 Asia Cup 2026 on Saturday, November 14. The highly anticipated summit clash is scheduled for 10:30 AM IST at the Al Amerat Cricket Ground (Ministry Turf 2). Both arch-rivals enter the final on the back of convincing semi-final victories, setting the stage for an exciting contest. Notably, Pakistan had previously defeated India in the group stages by three wickets, in their most recent fixture on November 08, 2026, adding another layer of intrigue to this championship encounter.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/pakistan-u19-to-face-india-u19-in-acc-mens-u19-asia-cup-2026.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India Under-19 secured their spot in the final with a dominant eight-wicket victory over Afghanistan Under-19 in the second semi-final. Chasing a target of 228 runs, the Boys in Blue comfortably reached the total in just 36.5 overs, with eight wickets to spare, showcasing their strong batting lineup. Pakistan Under-19, meanwhile, booked their place after registering a comprehensive nine-wicket victory against Bangladesh Under-19 in the first semi-final. They restricted Bangladesh to a mere 138 runs before chasing down the target in 21.5 overs, losing only one wicket. The Al Amerat Cricket Ground (Ministry Turf 2) surface is expected to offer assistance to pacers, particularly during the initial stages of the innings, suggesting batters will need to spend time at the crease on a slower pitch where stroke-making could be challenging.</p><p>Historically, India holds a slight edge in their head-to-head record against Pakistan in the U19 format. Out of 31 matches played, India U19 has won 17, while Pakistan U19 has claimed victory in 13 encounters, with one match resulting in no outcome. Their first-ever fixture dates back to March 02, 1988. Key individual performances could define the final, with India's opener Aaryavir Sehwag identified as a probable best batter. Sehwag has amassed an impressive 303 runs in four matches at an average of 101.00 and a strike rate of 95.58, hitting 29 boundaries and 16 sixes. For Pakistan, right-arm pacer Rizwanullah stands out as a probable best bowler, having taken 11 wickets in four matches at an average of 12.00.</p><p>The predicted playing 11 for India Under-19 includes Lakshya Rajesh Raichandani (c), Aaryavir Sehwag, VK Vineeth, Arjun Rajput, Yashbardhan Chauhan, Anvay Dravid (w), Manal Chauhan, Mohit Ulva, Aryan Savsani, Kavya Patel, and Ishan Sood. Pakistan Under-19's probable lineup features Usman Khan, Abdul Qadir, Farhan Yousaf (c), Ahmed Hussain, Ali Raza, Hamza Zahoor (w), Hasnain Abbas Dar, Mohammad Sayyam, Rizwanullah, Niqab Shafiq, and Hayam Khan. Based on expert analysis, the prediction for today's match suggests the team batting first is likely to win. The final will be broadcast live on Sony Sports Network Channels and streamed on SonyLIV (App &amp; Website).</p><p>What to watch: Expect a high-stakes battle between U19 arch-rivals on a pacer-friendly pitch.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes all provided data from the source text, including match statistics, player performance metrics, and historical context without adding unverified information.</p>
