     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana – Part I Smashes Rs. 1000 Crore Worldwide Box Office Milestone</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Box Office</span> <span>#Ramayana</span> <span>#Ranbir Kapoor</span></div>
       <p>The mythological epic &quot;Ramayana – Part I&quot;, starring Ranbir Kapoor and Yash, has made history by entering the prestigious Rs. 1000 crore worldwide club at the box office. Directed by Nitesh Tiwari, the film has become only the second Bollywood production of 2026 to achieve this remarkable feat, following &quot;Dhurandhar The Revenge&quot;. Its latest global collections stand at a staggering Rs. 1010.60 crores gross, firmly establishing it as one of the year's biggest box office successes.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/ramayana-part-i-smashes-rs-1000-crore-worldwide-box-office-m.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This significant achievement is particularly noteworthy as &quot;Ramayana&quot; was released on Thursday, November 5, and crossed the Rs. 1000 crore mark within its second week. The film has benefited from an extraordinary audience turnout during the post-Diwali period, coupled with substantial business generated from international markets, underscoring its broad appeal.</p><p>Detailed worldwide box office figures reveal &quot;Ramayana&quot; collected Rs. 543.09 crores nett in India, translating to domestic gross collections of Rs. 654.33 crores. Overseas territories contributed an impressive Rs. 356.27 crores gross, bringing the film’s total global earnings to Rs. 1010.60 crores. Interestingly, international markets account for approximately 35.25% of the film’s worldwide business, indicating that more than one-third of its global collections originated from outside India, while India contributed the remaining 64.75%.</p><p>The film’s success highlights a remarkable year for Bollywood, with two Hindi film productions managing to cross the four-digit crore mark globally. Earlier in 2026, &quot;Dhurandhar The Revenge&quot;, directed by Aditya Dhar, had also achieved the Rs. 1000 crore worldwide milestone. &quot;Ramayana – Part I&quot; joining this elite club further emphasizes the extraordinary scale of theatrical business witnessed throughout the year, marking a robust period for the industry.</p><p>What to watch: The continued impact of &quot;Ramayana&quot; on global box office trends.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the source text and provides a clear, accurate report.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/box-office-special-features/ramayana-worldwide-box-office-ranbir-kapoor-yash-epic-smashes-rs-1000-crore-milestone-becomes-only-the-second-bollywood-film-of-2026-after-dhurandhar-the-revenge-to-achieve-the-feat/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
