     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Royal Enfield owner wins ₹1 lakh compensation after motorcycle power loss</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The South Delhi Consumer Commission ordered Eicher Motors and Shree Mahadev Motors to pay ₹1 lakh to Hasan Murtaza, an Interceptor 650 owner. Murtaza alleged the bike suffered power loss during a 2021 Leh trip despite the dealer promising an ECU update before departure.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/royal-enfield-owner-wins-1-lakh-compensation-after-motorcycl.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Upon reaching Leh, a local service center confirmed the promised ECU update had not been performed. The commission ruled in favor of the owner after reviewing email correspondence and evidence, rejecting the manufacturer's claim that the dealer and parent company operated as entirely independent entities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and captures all essential details of the consumer dispute.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/leh-road-trip-turns-into-nightmare-for-royal-enfield-owner-after-bike-loses-power-how-he-won-1-lakh-in-consumer-court-11794546041733.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
