       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shivamogga to Host Under-16 Vijay Merchant Trophy Cricket Matches</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Under-16 Vijay Merchant Trophy cricket tournament will take place in Shivamogga from November 14 to December 8 at the KSCA and JNNCE Stadiums. Organized by the BCCI to foster young talent, the event features 36 teams divided into six groups. Shivamogga will host the Group C matches, which include teams from Chandigarh, Gujarat, Uttar Pradesh, Hyderabad, Haryana, and Odisha.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/shivamogga-to-host-under-16-vijay-merchant-trophy-cricket-ma.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The tournament will be inaugurated on Saturday at 8:30 a.m. with participation from local officials and KSCA representatives. Notably, local athlete Ayush Y.S. is representing the Karnataka team, which is currently competing in Group B.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is concise, accurate, and includes all necessary logistical details provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/vijay-merchant-trophy-cricket-matches-in-shivamogga/article71698524.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
