       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Mongabay India · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Teesta River flood survivors face ongoing displacement</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#environment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Three years after the 2023 Glacial Lake Outburst Flood (GLOF) caused by the South Lhonak Lake breach, survivors in Kalimpong remain in temporary relief camps. The disaster, which impacted 80,000 people and deposited 270 million cubic metres of sediment, significantly raised the Teesta riverbed.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/teesta-river-flood-survivors-face-ongoing-displacement.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Displaced residents report profound losses in social standing and independence, transitioning from stable lives to daily-wage labor. With consecutive flash floods in 2024 and 2025 further destabilizing the landscape, survivors continue to struggle on precarious land while facing the constant threat of recurring monsoon floods.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the social and economic impact of the Teesta River disaster using the provided figures.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://india.mongabay.com/2026/11/three-years-on-teestas-flood-survivors-live-in-limbo-as-the-river-creeps-closer/" rel="noopener">Mongabay India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
