       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-11-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Tejas Mk1A Handover to IAF Expected in January</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Tejas</span> <span>#IAF</span> <span>#Aero India</span></div>
       <p>The first Tejas Mk1A aircraft is likely to be delivered to the Indian Air Force (IAF) in January, according to an exclusive report by ThePrint. This significant development marks a key step in the indigenous fighter jet programme.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/tejas-mk1a-handover-to-iaf-expected-in-january.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The anticipated handover precedes the Aero India 2027 exhibition, suggesting a strategic timeline for the induction of the advanced light combat aircraft.</p><p>This information, attributed to ThePrint's exclusive coverage, details a crucial milestone for India's defence capabilities and aviation industry.</p><p>What to watch: Tejas Mk1A induction timeline.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the key details from the source summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
