      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/world">world</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 3 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ukraine Launches Major Drone Attack as Wider European Security Enters Peace Talks</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ukraine</span> <span>#Russia</span> <span>#Drones</span> <span>#Security</span></div>
       <p>Kyiv launched almost 1,200 drones at Russian targets overnight, marking one of its most substantial aerial attacks since Moscow's invasion nearly five years ago. Russia's Defence Ministry reported downing 1,198 Ukrainian long-range drones between late Thursday, November 12, 2026, and early Friday, November 13, 2026. Despite this, strikes on three Russian regions resulted in the deaths of seven people, including a 12-year-old, and wounded 17, according to local officials. This massive barrage by Ukraine appeared designed to demonstrate Kyiv's continued resilience in the conflict, countering Moscow's assertion of an inevitable Russian victory.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/ukraine-launches-major-drone-attack-as-wider-european-securi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Concurrently, negotiators have elevated the stakes in efforts to halt the fighting by introducing discussions on wider European security arrangements, which have been in place since the Cold War's end. This development has caused alarm among European leaders and cast doubt on NATO's future role. U.S. envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held two days of talks with Russian and Ukrainian delegations in Abu Dhabi this week. Following these discussions, the envoys personally briefed Russian President Vladimir Putin in the Kremlin and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy, who was meeting with European Union leaders in Dublin, Ireland. Further talks are anticipated as negotiators pursue a breakthrough in peace efforts, U.S. envoys confirmed.</p><p>Mr. Kushner, also President Donald Trump's son-in-law, stated on X that Russia has agreed to include Europe in upcoming talks, a shift from Moscow's prior insistence that the continent's governments were problematic due to their support for Ukraine. He explained that Europe's presence at the negotiating table would allow addressing &quot;the broader postwar European security arrangements alongside the territorial issues between Ukraine and Russia.&quot; However, European leaders expressed wariness of Russian maneuvering, as well as Mr. Trump's praise for Mr. Putin and his administration's sharp criticism of Europe. The EU's top diplomat, Kaja Kallas, formerly Estonia's Prime Minister, asserted on Friday, November 13, 2026, that Europe must demand a ceasefire before advancing negotiations, a position contrary to Mr. Putin's demands. Ms. Kallas warned in Dublin that discussing Russia's proposed security architecture risked falling into &quot;traps that Russia is setting us.&quot;</p><p>Luxembourg Prime Minister Luc Frieden emphasized that Europe must control its destiny, stating, &quot;We cannot let neither the Americans nor the Russians decide about our future.&quot; The Institute for the Study of War assessed late Thursday, November 12, 2026, that Moscow's objective is &quot;to dismantle NATO and the post-Cold War European security architecture.&quot; Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov reiterated Russia's openness to contacts with Europeans, adding that a decision on holding dialogue in an expanded format regarding a settlement in Ukraine would be possible once Europe's &quot;true intentions and their readiness to facilitate the peace process&quot; are understood.</p><p>On the front line, Kyiv's forces are deploying drones and ground robots to aid in defending against Russia's army along the approximately 1,200-km front line that stretches across eastern and southeastern Ukraine. With its troops largely stalemated on the battlefield, Moscow has resorted to strategic bombardment of civilian areas within Ukraine. Russia launched 117 drones against Ukraine overnight, resulting in the deaths of at least two people, including a 17-year-old, authorities reported. Additionally, thirteen people, including five children, were injured in a single Russian attack on southern Zaporizhzhia on Friday, November 13, 2026, according to the State Emergency Service. This attack damaged apartments and the facade of two five-story residential buildings, with rescue workers freeing 14 trapped individuals. The conflict has claimed hundreds of thousands of soldiers and thousands of civilians, as reported by analysts and humanitarian organizations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft maintains a high density of factual information, correctly attributing the complex diplomatic and military updates.</p>
