     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-11-13 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Union Minister Nirmala Sitharaman launches 'Bharat Vann' project in Mysuru</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman inaugurated the 'Bharat Vann' project in Mysuru on November 13, aimed at expanding the city's green cover. Supported by the SBI Foundation, the initiative involves planting two lakh native saplings across the city, with 45,000 trees slated for K.C. Layout Park.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/union-minister-nirmala-sitharaman-launches-bharat-vann-proje.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Implementing organizations, including Catch Foundation and Enviro Creators Foundation, have committed to maintaining the saplings for three years to ensure survival. The project, which also involves plantation activities in Vijayanagar, seeks to boost biodiversity, improve air quality, and enhance the urban ecosystem through collaboration with the Mysuru City Corporation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the project scope, implementation, and objectives without unnecessary padding.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/bharat-vann-project-launched-to-boost-mysurus-green-cover/article71696792.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/mysuru/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mysuru</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
