     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-11-13 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Yogi Adityanath Proposes 'One District, One Art' Initiative</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Uttar Pradesh Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath has proposed a 'One District, One Art' initiative to preserve the state's traditional arts and create sustainable livelihoods for performers. Modeled after existing successful programs like 'One District, One Product,' the initiative aims to identify unique regional art forms and provide artists with consistent platforms to showcase their talent.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-11-13/yogi-adityanath-proposes-one-district-one-art-initiative.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Adityanath encouraged the use of technology and digital media to reach global audiences while maintaining cultural roots. The state's Culture Department is tasked with supporting regular public performances to ensure these traditions remain vibrant, economically viable, and a source of pride for future generations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise, accurate summary of the proposed policy and its objectives.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
